[{:adr/consequences "{:no_behavior_change \"name-only rename; kotoba.turn.credential's newly-added\\n                       mint-credential-scoped/verify-credential-scoped (commit 2d90bddc)\\n                       ship under org-ietf-turn from this point forward\", :kami_engine_sdk_unaffected \"turn.ts does not yet delegate to a compiled bridge from\\n                               org-ietf-turn -- remains explicit follow-up per\\n                               ADR-2607052000, unaffected by this rename\", :naming_caveat \"rt and net now carry names that could be misread as claiming full\\n                 external-spec conformance (WebRTC, libp2p) they explicitly disclaim in\\n                 their own ADRs -- consumers should read the repo's own docs/ADR-*.md\\n                 before assuming spec completeness from the name alone\"}", :adr/authoritative_for ["kotoba-lang/turn -> kotoba-lang/org-ietf-turn (IETF RFC 8656 TURN message layer),\n    kotoba-lang/signal -> kotoba-lang/org-signal (Signal Protocol, signal.org),\n    kotoba-lang/rt -> kotoba-lang/org-w3-webrtc-signaling (NOT a spec port -- kotoba's own\n    room-routing contract, named after the WebRTC signaling concept it relays),\n    kotoba-lang/net -> kotoba-lang/io-libp2p (NOT a libp2p port -- explicitly simplified\n    GossipSub/Bitswap-inspired semantics only, named after libp2p.io per owner direction --\n    first repo using a literal-TLD io-<name> prefix, distinct from org-<body>-<spec> and\n    the compat-catalog's unconditional com-<vendor>)" "GitHub repos renamed (redirects preserved), local checkouts moved + remotes retargeted,\n    manifest/repos.edn (:path-overrides + :extra-projects) and manifest/west.yml updated\n    and pin-verified, landed via GitHub Contents API single-entry commits directly to main\n    (no PR, per :manifest-workflow)" "no deps.edn dependents existed for any of the 4 repos -- no downstream code changes\n    needed" "org-ietf-turn's pin (2d90bddc) includes the room/player-scoped credential increment\n    from this session's earlier ADR-2607052000 work -- caught a stale local checkout before\n    landing and fast-forwarded it first" "a concurrent session's unrelated claude-lmstudio manifest entry was caught mid-operation\n    and preserved by rebuilding the rename diff against the latest GitHub tip rather than a\n    slightly-stale local copy"], :adr/supersedes [], :adr/superseded_by [], :adr/topic "kotoba-lang-turn-rt-net-signal-rename", :adr/related ["90-docs/adr/2607052000-kami-engine-sdk-svelte-retirement-cljs-migration.md" "90-docs/adr/2607051200-kotoba-lang-ui-family-rename.md" "90-docs/adr/2607041500-etzhayyim-compat-catalog-to-kotoba-lang.md"], :adr/status "accepted", :adr/id "adr-2607052300-kotoba-lang-turn-rt-net-signal-reverse-domain-rename", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-05", :adr/decision "{:renames [{:old \"turn\", :new \"org-ietf-turn\", :rationale \"IETF RFC 8656 (TURN) message layer -- clean spec port, same org-ietf-oauth2\\n                precedent (RFC-numbered IETF spec)\"} {:old \"signal\", :new \"org-signal\", :rationale \"Signal Protocol (signal.org) -- clean spec port, org name is the qualifier\\n                (org-openusd/org-materialx shape, no further -<spec> suffix needed)\"} {:old \"rt\", :new \"org-w3-webrtc-signaling\", :rationale \"NOT a spec port per its own ADR -- kotoba's own room-routing contract,\\n                named after the broader WebRTC signaling concept (W3C) it relays, per\\n                owner direction\"} {:old \"net\", :new \"io-libp2p\", :rationale \"NOT a libp2p port per its own ADR -- explicitly simplified GossipSub/\\n                Bitswap-inspired semantics only. Named after libp2p.io (literal-TLD\\n                reverse-domain io-<name> form) per owner direction -- distinct from\\n                org-<body>-<spec> and the compat-catalog's unconditional com-<vendor>\\n                (ADR-2607041500). First repo using this io- prefix; not yet a general\\n                doctrine.\"}], :deliberate_distinction \"two of the four (rt, net) are explicitly NOT external-spec ports per their own ADRs --\\n   their new names describe the domain/concept they relate to, not spec conformance they\\n   don't have. Should not be flattened in future renames: a repo's name must never claim\\n   more spec conformance than its own ADR documents.\", :execution {:steps [\"gh repo rename x4 (GitHub preserves old-name redirects)\" \"local checkout dir moved + remote retargeted, x4\" \"dependent repos: none found (grep across orgs/**/deps.edn for\\n            kotoba-lang/{turn,rt,net,signal} or matching :local/root paths -- zero hits)\" \"manifest/repos.edn: 4 new :path-overrides entries + 4 :extra-projects lines\\n            updated to new paths\" \"manifest/west.yml: nbb scripts/gen-west-manifest.cljs --entry\\n            org-ietf-turn,org-w3-webrtc-signaling,io-libp2p,org-signal (server-side pin\\n            verify OK), old 4 entries manually removed (--entry doesn't delete). Net\\n            project count unchanged (1462->1462), pure rename.\" \"landed via GitHub Contents API single-entry commits directly to main, no\\n            branch/PR, per :manifest-workflow\"], :caught_before_landing [\"local org-ietf-turn checkout was one commit stale (missing the room/player-scoped-\\n     credential increment merged to main earlier this session) -- fast-forwarded before\\n     regenerating that entry's pin\" \"a concurrent session pushed an unrelated claude-lmstudio manifest entry mid-operation\\n     -- rebuilt the surgical rename diff against the latest GitHub tip instead of the\\n     slightly-stale local working copy, so that entry wasn't silently dropped\"]}}", :db/id -1, :adr/problem "{:source \"surfaced while landing ADR-2607052000's first concrete increment (extending\\n           kotoba.turn.credential with a room/player-scoped mint/verify variant) -- the\\n           bare names turn/rt/net/signal don't self-document which external spec (if any)\\n           each repo implements, unlike the already-established org-<body>-<spec> family\", :investigated [\"read each repo's own docs/ADR-kotoba-{turn,rt,net,signal}-*.md in full before deciding\\n    a name, specifically to avoid overclaiming spec conformance in the name itself -- same\\n    failure mode the org-taxonomy rule already guards against (com-apple-{touchid,faceid}\\n    correctly uses the vendor com- scheme, not org-, because Apple's LocalAuthentication is\\n    proprietary not a published open spec)\" \"kotoba-lang/turn's ADR: message layer of IETF RFC 8656 (TURN) -- credential mint/verify\\n    (coturn use-auth-secret), STUN RFC 8489 codec, MESSAGE-INTEGRITY, FINGERPRINT. Clean\\n    external-spec port.\" \"kotoba-lang/signal's ADR: the Signal Protocol (X3DH -> Double Ratchet, sender-keys\\n    group ratchet), signal.org. Clean external-spec port, org name IS the spec name (same\\n    shape as org-openusd/org-materialx).\" \"kotoba-lang/rt's ADR is explicit: 'this is deliberately NOT a WebSocket server' --\\n    kotoba's own room-membership/route-message contract, not a port of any single numbered\\n    external spec\" \"kotoba-lang/net's ADR is explicit: 're-implementing the entire libp2p stack... is not\\n    realistic' -- only loosely models GossipSub/Bitswap semantics as simplified pure-data\\n    functions, not a conformant libp2p port\"], :risk \"a repo name overclaiming spec conformance it doesn't have is worse than a boring\\n         bare name, since the name becomes the (mis)documentation\"}", :adr/alternatives [], :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607052300: kotoba-lang -- rename turn/rt/net/signal to reverse-domain\n          external-spec names"}]